From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: clear stale lane ready flags before starting the link

0010 waits for CLK_LANE_RDY and DATA_LANE_RDY(i) in MCTL_MAIN_STS
without clearing them first, and mainline does the same. The same driver
does clear PLL_LOCKED in MCTL_MAIN_STS_CLR before activating the PLL.

On Astrial H15 the lane wait measures about 262 ms on the first modeset
after boot, on every boot, and 0 us on every modeset after that,
including right after PLL and lanes had been stopped by hand at register
level. That is what flags left over from the previous bring-up look
like. With them uncleared, no lane measurement after the first one can be
trusted.

Clear the lane flags together with PLL_LOCKED, which is before the PHY
is powered and before the lane resets are released. Not right before the
poll in bridge_enable: the lanes come up during pre_enable, so clearing
there would erase an event that has already happened and make the poll
time out on every cycle whether or not anything is wrong. Placed here,
the measurement is correct whether those bits are live status or latched
flags.

After this patch a "Timed Out: DSI-DPhy Clock and Data Lanes not ready"
message is a measurement, not a regression.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -714,7 +714,8 @@
 static void cdns_dsi_hs_init(struct cdns_dsi *dsi)
 {
 	struct cdns_dsi_output *output = &dsi->output;
-	u32 status;
+	u32 status, stale;
+	int i;
 	
 	if (dsi->phy_initialized)
 		return;
@@ -733,7 +734,10 @@
 	phy_power_on(dsi->dphy);
 
 	/* Activate the PLL and wait until it's locked. */
-	writel(PLL_LOCKED, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_STS_CLR);
+	stale = PLL_LOCKED | CLK_LANE_RDY;
+	for (i = 0; i < output->dev->lanes; i++)
+		stale |= DATA_LANE_RDY(i);
+	writel(stale, dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_STS_CLR);
 	writel(DPHY_CMN_PSO | DPHY_ALL_D_PDN | DPHY_C_PDN | DPHY_CMN_PDN,
 	       dsi->regs + MCTL_DPHY_CFG0);
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(readl_poll_timeout(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_STS, status,
